#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152178 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e049969f-d389-5d67-a96c-4e0430942925" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Local Extrema of a Function Visually"}] :question/id #uuid "986cc1f3-747e-53cb-845d-411a21c9bc23" :question/math-academy-id "e-6683" :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown below. Which of the points shown are the local maxima of the function?\n\n![](images/24/245ba0a543188d50e52c23c854f9f82290790ed715c241bf27e505b04d857a4e.png)" :question/worked-solution "Consider the point $U$. We can take an open interval of $x$-values such that $U$ will be the highest point on the graph in this interval. So, $U$ is a local maximum.\n\nA similar interval exists for the point $W$, too. So, $W$ is also a local maximum.\n\n![](images/ac/ac0a6e28e4564883e6743b2d600cb8611723e813e85c1acb5fcc327ee3dbc9b5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152026 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152216 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "05fd062c-7474-5f4d-aa40-06913fb420df" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Local Extrema of a Function Using a Condition"}] :question/id #uuid "fa76f558-adeb-5d8d-9273-70f2d8a76f97" :question/math-academy-id "e-7970" :question/problem "For which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y = f(x)$, shown below, attain a local minimum?\n\n1. $x=0$\n2. $x=1$\n3. $x=3$\n\n![](images/17/1718b48d39255b221037a439cc48d300a04c33ffb4e04c700fefb303a20ebff2.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given points in turn.\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=0$. For example, in the interval $(-0.5,0.5)$, the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=0$, as shown below.![](images/e2/e25e6e31d6ea5d7f882d4eed16c82ec8280d1ed56f275974e8f07091c0e62c5d.png)\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(0) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-0.5,0.5)$.\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=1$. For any open interval containing $x=1$, there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(1)$.\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=3$. For example, in the interval $(2.5,3.5)$, the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=3$, as shown below.![](images/d1/d133d7ee4c022b47740f62b8e73ba9ea2f70e788861c25d2824b5e7236027c60.png)\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(3) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (2.5,3.5)$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152027 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152217 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9296cdb-31d8-5855-b605-a47c33b21c85" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding a Function's Local Extrema"}] :question/id #uuid "2cfd4563-e033-50c6-8e39-55295e81b4da" :question/math-academy-id "e-7971" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the function shown below. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=-2$\n2. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=2$\n3. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=0$\n\n![](images/9b/9b933b1b869b74f2a7340f9ba4034b970c49434d12592d3ff1e152057b6adef1.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a local minimum at $x=-2$. For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5)$, the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-2$, as shown below.![](images/3a/3abb7470db51fa1bdb61e15aec1739de44bf5083b7341b90a65ac93fc7f8adbb.png)\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(-2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-2.5,-1.5)$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=2$. For example, in the interval $(1.5,2.5)$, the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=2$, as shown below.![](images/71/71c6e7af0a1de77543b57d2aee242fe84295ad46c748b2f65f7cba381c47b80c.png)\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (1.5,2.5)$.\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=0$. For example, in the interval $(-0.5,0.5)$, the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=0$, as shown below.![](images/83/83de300c3e00766d46989d12b4e1708ef9a73f4d02748009a526b1646d7f0b81.png)\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\le f(0) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-0.5,0.5)$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152028 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152218 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c98ce69-8410-51a4-8d9c-eec7b46fb83b" :knowledge-point/title "Global vs. Local Extrema"}] :question/id #uuid "10bb268e-60a2-5e88-9c78-f26dc11db1a7" :question/math-academy-id "e-7972" :question/problem "The graph of a function $y = f(x)$ is shown below. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=2$\n2. $f(x)$ attains a **global** maximum at $x=0$\n3. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=-2$\n\n![](images/91/91d9d4997dd58c2c3cb07efc1529487bbd9a5a2f5c611054289cfc2ba24d764c.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=2$. For example, in the interval $(1.5,2.5)$, the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=2$, as shown below.![](images/00/00a21a670b2080ce766ddf142eb2f37303d7af7b667e1b5038eee93879c071f7.png)\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (1.5,2.5)$.\n- Statement II is false. The function does *not* have a global maximum at $x=0$. The global maximum is the highest point on the graph, but our function has points where its value is greater than $f(0)$. For example, $f(0) \\lt f(3)$.\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=-2$. For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5)$, the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-2$, as shown below.![](images/fc/fc96fe5bb938b0ca8569b864588348a4d22280e3c4a5806cdd20af6eb4bcea34.png)\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(-2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-2.5,-1.5)$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152589 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152178 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e049969f-d389-5d67-a96c-4e0430942925" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Local Extrema of a Function Visually"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d151b65c-7599-5f10-b2e9-38c668d78ecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $D$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150042} {:answer/id #uuid "1a63a993-065b-5cdd-8e51-f3139c3a0a0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The function does not have local maxima" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150043} {:answer/id #uuid "46c70979-98ae-5507-8da7-032906d837fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D$ and $E$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150044} {:answer/id #uuid "4af94f20-7dad-5307-99ba-1ce48715b2c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $E$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150045} {:answer/id #uuid "4ebff280-1d8a-5d72-acd3-f2be15432d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$, $C$, and $E$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150046}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7a689b3a-bf48-5ac5-ac02-0304f48ba3a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150041}] :question/id #uuid "28dd7636-555e-56f2-95d9-58a422ebb093" :question/math-academy-id "q-37218" :question/problem "![](images/20/20b6e19fcb7e1fe4f33697d517c28d9563c793634cfbcd5552d842efeef3ef61.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y = f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the points shown are the local maxima of the function?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152216 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "05fd062c-7474-5f4d-aa40-06913fb420df" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Local Extrema of a Function Using a Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1809cb8-fdc2-5574-8f0a-5a6c7ab0cb37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150072} {:answer/id #uuid "abc4ca59-2348-58fc-ab82-f9db7daa69e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150073} {:answer/id #uuid "bc9a2ec5-9d5a-53f9-9125-061ed3b6d2b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150074} {:answer/id #uuid "d935d618-f8fe-5fd5-8492-932d981427ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150075} {:answer/id #uuid "77d44d72-e2f8-5440-ac87-43247e745bd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150076}] :answer-field/id #uuid "92ba2275-3203-5d26-ae0c-577da6431af2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150071}] :question/id #uuid "73bf3b03-b88e-5d7f-a6de-e6310c1e255b" :question/math-academy-id "q-37834" :question/problem "![](images/c4/c46e88b9e044fccb91e0efa4ee981973a286e0335f58a70f7b1f9a856d9bfed4.png)\n\nFor which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y = f(x)$, shown above, attain a local minimum?\n\n1. $x = 3$\n2. $x = 2$\n3. $x =-2$"}]}
